Subject: [PATCH 139/230] feat(bot): one tap from a push to the match it is
 about
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A goal push named the match but pointed nowhere: the user either opened
the app and hunted for it, or muted the bot. Goal alerts and the whole
matchday fan-out now end with a per-language footer line and a
/#/match/<id> Mini App deep link, built at queue time from
MINI_APP_URL — with the env unset or still a placeholder (example.com)
the copy stays bare, never a dead link (tests pin both shapes).

The drain also logs pushes delivered more than 120s after queueing:
latency is exactly what makes the push channel feel untrustworthy mid-
match, so it is measured at the one place where it is visible.

